! The orbital magnetization of `i-atom-soc.in`, by `pw.x`'s own route.
!
! `lorbm = .true.` in a non-self-consistent run over a uniform grid is what
! reaches `PW/src/orbm_kubo.f90`, which prints the two Kubo terms in Bohr
! magnetons per cell. It is norm-conserving only (`setup.f90` refuses ultrasoft
! and PAW) and it sums every band it is given with no occupations at all, so
! `nbnd = 7` here is the occupied manifold and nothing else -- which is also why
! the manifold has to be gapped for the number to mean anything.
!
! Three divisions per direction is the smallest uniform grid that carries a
! derivative: with two, a point's two neighbours along a direction are the same
! k-point and every difference is identically zero.
!
! `pw.x` builds its own k-grid for this (`kpoint_grid_efield`) and sets
! `nosym`, so the K_POINTS card below only says how many divisions.
 &control
    calculation = 'nscf'
    lorbm = .true.
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 1, celldm(1) = 12.0, nat = 1, ntyp = 1, ecutwfc = 45.0,
    occupations = 'fixed', nbnd = 7,
    noncolin = .true., lspinorb = .true.,
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.5, angle1(1) = 0.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 I 126.9 I.rel-pbe-nc-dojo.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 I 0.00 0.00 0.00
K_POINTS (automatic)
 3 3 3 0 0 0
